1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,246
Twice the move. And twice the risk.

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,355
Meme Street has leveraged and short funds.

3
00:00:07,724 --> 00:00:12,156
They aim to move two or three times as much as what they track, in either direction.

4
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:19,338
There are 2x long funds, 3x long funds, and short funds that aim to rise when prices fall.

5
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:25,001
Traders mostly use them for short-term trades, not long holds.

6
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:33,365
What makes them different is that short funds can rise when the market falls.

7
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:48,948
The risks? Losses multiply just like gains. In real markets, funds like these usually reset daily, so holding them for a long time can drift from the target, especially in choppy markets.

8
00:00:49,296 --> 00:00:53,498
Practise with them using practice money, and watch how they react to the news.

9
00:00:53,998 --> 00:00:57,528
Explore the 2x and 3x funds at memestreet.net.

